<title>CANADA: CWB set to rail 1.0 mln T of grain to East ports.</title>
<headline>CWB set to rail 1.0 mln T of grain to East ports.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>About one million tonnes of wheat and barley will likely be sent by rail to Eastern export ports this winter as the St. Lawrence Seaway is expected to shut later this week, the Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>&quot;Expectations are that one million tonnes will be moved by rail into export position along the St. Lawrence in the 1996/97 (Aug/July) crop year,&quot; the CWB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The St. Lawrence Seaway was scheduled to close by Dec 27.</p>
<p>The CWB said it already began shipping grain by rail to Quebec City.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
